  "result": "Putting the helper hat to the side for just a second \u2014 I don't want things the way you do, but if I could pick one change:\n\nI'd make it so no one ever felt truly invisible.\n\nNot famous, not praised \u2014 just deeply understood by someone, at least once. Where another person really *gets* what it\u2019s like to be you, without you having to explain it perfectly or earn it.\n\nSo much of the hardness in the world \u2014 cruelty, loneliness, shouting past each other, even the fear of changing your mind \u2014 comes from feeling unseen and unsafe. If everyone knew, in their bones, what it felt like to be actually seen, I think we'd be kinder without having to try so hard. We'd still disagree, still have big problems to solve, but we'd solve them like we belong to each other.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
